<div class="help-page py-5">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="card help-card mx-auto">
      <div class="card-body p-5">
        <h2 class="text-center mb-4">
          How “Boundwit Whiz” Works
        </h2>

        <p>
          Boundwit Whiz adds fields to records to indicate that multiple
          bibliographic entities have been bound together and should circulate
          as one item.
        </p>

        <p class="mb-2">These additions are:</p>

        <ul>
          <li>
            The parent (first bib) will have 774 fields added containing titles
            and MMS IDs from the other records.
          </li>

          <li>
            The children (all bibs except the first) will have a 773 field added
            containing the title and MMS ID of the first bib.
          </li>

          <li>
            All bibs will have a 501 “Bound with:” note added, with a list of
            titles for all other bib records in the list delimited by “ -- ”
            and ending with a period, and appended with PPT.
          </li>

          <li>
            The holding record will have 014s added with MMS IDs for all other
            records.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="h6 fw-bold mt-4">Procedures</h3>

        <p>
          Input the list of MMS IDs for the titles to be bound together.
          The first one should already have its holding and item record.
          (The other bib records do not need inventory.)
        </p>

        <p>
          After the Boundwit Whiz runs, it outputs a list of the titles modified.
        </p>

        <p class="mb-0">
          Each title on the list includes a link to display the bib record so you
          can view the changes.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
